DP  - 2018 Dec
TI  - Transbronchial Cryobiopsies.
PG  - 637-648
LID - 10.1055/s-0038-1676645 [doi]
AB  - Transbronchial lung cryobiopsy (TBLCB) is a relatively new and promising 
      technique for the acquisition of larger amounts of higher quality lung tissue for 
      the diagnosis of lung diseases. There is a growing body of literature describing 
      a diagnostic yield comparable to surgical lung biopsy with a favorable safety 
      profile. Due to its advantages TBLCB has garnered significant interest with more 
      institutions beginning to adopt this technique. However, several questions remain 
      including its role in the diagnostic algorithm, indications, and technique. 
      Herein we provide a review of the available literature describing diagnostic 
      yield, complications, and differing techniques as well as a perspective from 
      pathology.
