TI  - Cryobiopsy for Secondary Pulmonary Alveolar Proteinosis.
PG  - e60530
LID - 10.7759/cureus.60530 [doi]
LID - e60530
AB  - Secondary pulmonary alveolar proteinosis (SPAP) is one of the diffuse parenchymal 
      lung diseases, and the utility and safety of transbronchial lung cryobiopsy 
      (TBLC) for diagnosing SPAP are unknown. A case of SPAP diagnosed by TBLC is 
      presented. Specimens that were useful for diagnosis were collected, and there was 
      no adverse event following TBLC. The usefulness of TBLC for interstitial lung 
      disease has been widely reported, but there are few reports of SPAP. We present 
      the clinical course of TBLC in the diagnosis of SPAP.
