TI  - [Transbronchial cryobiopsies: an alternative for surgical lung biopsy].
LID - D5499 [pii]
AB  - Cryobiopsy is an endobronchial technique to obtain peripheral lung biopsies with 
      the use of a flexible bronchoscopic cryo probe. This technique can be used to 
      diagnose diffuse lung diseases when histological evidence is required. This new 
      technique was used for the first time in 2009 and in 2014 we introduced this new 
      method in the Netherlands at the CWZ in Nijmegen. This piece outlines our 
      experiences with Transbronchial lung cryobiopsy (TBLC).
