PMID- 41850831
OWN - NLM
STAT- Publisher
LR  - 20260318
IS  - 1349-7235 (Electronic)
IS  - 0918-2918 (Linking)
DP  - 2026 Mar 17
TI  - A Case of Methotrexate-induced Other Iatrogenic Immunodeficiency-associated 
      Lymphoproliferative Disorder with Diffuse Ground-glass Opacities Diagnosed Using 
      a Cryobiopsy.
LID - 10.2169/internalmedicine.6755-25 [doi]
AB  - Methotrexate (MTX)-induced iatrogenic immunodeficiency-associated 
      lymphoproliferative disorder (OIIA-LPD) usually presents as multiple pulmonary 
      nodules or masses. However, we herein present a rare case demonstrating diffuse 
      ground-glass opacities (GGOs). The patient was a 77-year-old woman with a history 
      of rheumatoid arthritis and advanced gastric cancer. Because of the markedly 
      elevated serum lactate dehydrogenase levels and diffuse GGOs on chest computed 
      tomography, intravascular lymphoma was considered. A transbronchial lung 
      cryobiopsy (TBLC) was performed to obtain tissue specimens for a 
      histopathological evaluation, leading to a diffuse large B-cell lymphoma 
      diagnosis after multidisciplinary discussions. To the best of our knowledge, this 
      is the first report of MTX-induced OIIA-LPD diagnosed by TBLC.
